# Commit Types: feat / content / fix

## When to use each type

| Type | Use for | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| `feat` | New features, UI components, functionality | `feat: add artist grid component` |
| `content` | Text, copy, media, data - no code logic change | `content: update band bios` |
| `fix` | Bug fixes, error handling, corrections | `fix: resolve mobile menu overflow` |

---

## Other valid types

| Type | Use for |
|------|--------|
| `refactor` | Internal improvements without changing behavior |
| `style` | Visual adjustments (CSS, spacing, UI tweaks) |
| `docs` | Documentation updates |
| `chore` | Tooling, config, non-feature maintenance |

## feat (feature)

- New components, pages, or functionality
- New UI/UX elements
- New integrations or APIs

**Branch**: `feature/<kebab-case-name>` from develop  
**Commit**: `feat: short description`

---

## content

- Text, headlines, descriptions
- Images, audio, media assets
- Mock data, band info, events

**Branch**: `content/<kebab-case-name>` from develop (or direct on develop for small edits)  
**Commit**: `content: short description`

---

## fix

- Bug fixes
- Error handling
- Layout or behavior corrections

**Branch**: `fix/<kebab-case-name>` from develop  
**Commit**: `fix: short description`
